WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.362
Hi! Which of two four-digit numbers is greater? Today we'll compare numbers, put them in order and find number patterns.

2
00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:18.450
Compare 4815 and 4581. First the thousands: both are 4, so they're the same.

3
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.626
Next, the hundreds: 8 is greater than 5.

4
00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:31.386
So 4815 is greater than 4581. The open side of the sign faces the greater number.

5
00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:44.610
Ordering 3409, 3940 and 3049 from smallest to greatest gives 3049, 3409, 3940.

6
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.994
Look at 1250, 1450, 1650. What comes next?

7
00:00:51.144 --> 00:00:54.882
Each number is 200 more than the one before.

8
00:00:55.032 --> 00:01:01.626
So the next number is 1650 plus 200, which is 1850.

9
00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:09.402
To find a pattern, work out the gap between neighbouring numbers, then see if they go up or down.

10
00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:18.450
Watch out! Some pupils see that 0 is less than 9 in the ones place and say 3940 is smaller. That's wrong!

11
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:28.602
We compare from the biggest place. The thousands are the same, and in the hundreds 9 is greater than 4, so 3940 is greater.

12
00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:34.962
Once a bigger place decides it, we don't need to look at the smaller places.

13
00:01:35.112 --> 00:01:47.778
Your turn! Which is greater, 5762 or 5726? Pause and think.

14
00:01:47.928 --> 00:02:01.698
The thousands and hundreds are the same. In the tens, 6 is greater than 2, so 5762 is greater than 5726. Did you get it right?

15
00:02:01.848 --> 00:02:13.506
Another one! 2300, 2250, 2200. What comes next? Pause and think.

16
00:02:13.656 --> 00:02:21.594
It goes down by 50 each time, so the next number is 2150. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:21.744 --> 00:02:31.770
Here's another! What is 1000 more than 6450? Pause and think.

18
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:40.962
The thousands digit goes up by 1. The answer is 7450. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:41.112 --> 00:02:52.074
Here's another! Use 5, 0, 8 and 3 to make the greatest four-digit number. Pause and think.

20
00:02:52.224 --> 00:03:01.050
Put the biggest digit in the biggest place, from greatest to smallest: 8530. Did you get it right?

21
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:13.218
Last one! Which is the smallest: 6008, 6080 or 6800? Pause and think.

22
00:03:13.368 --> 00:03:23.826
All have 6 thousands. Two have 0 hundreds, so compare the tens: 6008 is the smallest. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:32.610
Remember: to compare numbers, start from the biggest place. To find a pattern, first work out the gap between neighbouring numbers.

24
00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:38.082
Next time you see house numbers, compare which is greater!

